# scriptsquid.dev

Portfolio and blog for a senior systems administrator moving into security. Brand: ScriptSquid. Tagline: "I automate infrastructure, then try to break it."

- Astro static output, TypeScript, plain CSS custom properties. No Tailwind.
- Posts, projects, and page copy live in `src/content` (Markdown/MDX collections). Do not hardcode that content in components.
- Deploy target: Netlify, linked to the GitHub repo `xScriptSquid/squidsite` (`npm run build`, output `dist`, Node 22).

Design:

- Dark theme by default. Light theme only through `prefers-color-scheme`.
- One accent, teal/cyan around `#2dd4bf`. No neon green, no Matrix effects.
- Space Grotesk for headings. Inter for body. JetBrains Mono for terminal accents, code, kicker labels, and dates. Self-host all three. Do not load fonts from a third party at runtime.
- Prose max-width about 720px. Grids max-width about 1280px. Leave generous whitespace.
- Terminal cues stay subtle: prompt labels like `~/projects`, and a blinking cursor in the hero only.

Engineering:

- No client-side JavaScript unless a feature cannot work without it. Pages must stay readable with JavaScript disabled.
- Semantic HTML. WCAG AA contrast, visible focus, alt text on images.
- No third-party trackers.
- Keep components small. Site identity (name, role, tagline) lives in `src/config.ts`.
